Fixed. The bug was in `src/import_merge.ts:7` — the duplicate check compared URLs with `===`, which is case-sensitive, so `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` never matched.

The fix normalizes each URL by lowercasing its hostname (hostnames are case-insensitive per the URL spec) before comparison. Same-URL case variants now merge into the existing entry with unioned tags; still returns 1 entry with tags `["x","y"]`. Non-URL strings fall back to plain lowercasing.


